---
title: Compaction
id: compaction
order: 3
description: "Keep long chats under the context limit with @tanstack/ai-compaction. withCompaction runs a pluggable strategy before each model call: evict, summarize, or clear old tool output."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - compaction
  - context window
  - middleware
  - token limit
  - summarize history
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A long chat or a multi-step agent loop keeps adding messages. At some point the transcript passes the model's context limit and the call fails. You want the conversation to keep working without hitting that wall."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withCompaction"},{"type":"text","value":" shrinks provider context before each model call. When the context passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":", a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"strategy"}]},{"type":"text","value":" rewrites what the model sees. The canonical transcript does not change. Add this "},{"type":"link","href":"./middleware","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatMiddleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware"},{"type":"text","value":" array of any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/ai-compaction","lang":"bash"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick start"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default strategy drops the oldest messages once the transcript passes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" and keeps the recent ones."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { withCompaction } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withCompaction({ maxTokens: 100_000 })],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"pick-a-strategy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pick a strategy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strategy"},{"type":"text","value":" to change how the history shrinks. Three are built in."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it does"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cost"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"evictOldest"},{"type":"text","value":" (default)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drop the oldest messages, leave a marker"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No extra model call"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarizeOldest"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Replace the oldest messages with an LLM summary"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One summarize call"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clearToolResults"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stub the content of old tool results, keep the messages"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No extra model call"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"evictoldest","children":[{"type":"text","value":"evictOldest"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cheapest. Keeps the recent tail, drops the older head, and leaves a short marker in its place. This is the default, so you only name it to tune "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keepRecentTokens"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { withCompaction, evictOldest } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: evictOldest({ keepRecentTokens: 40_000 }),\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"summarizeoldest","children":[{"type":"text","value":"summarizeOldest"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keeps the gist of old turns instead of dropping them, at the cost of one summarization call. Pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize"},{"type":"text","value":" callback. It gets the messages about to be dropped and returns the summary text. Wire it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize()"},{"type":"text","value":" or any model call."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, summarize, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText, openaiSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { withCompaction, summarizeOldest } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function summarizeHistory(messages: Array<ModelMessage>): Promise<string> {\n  const text = messages\n    .map((m) => `${m.role}: ${typeof m.content === \"string\" ? m.content : \"\"}`)\n    .join(\"\\n\");\n\n  const { summary } = await summarize({\n    adapter: openaiSummarize(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    text,\n  });\n  return summary;\n}\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [\n      withCompaction({\n        maxTokens: 100_000,\n        strategy: summarizeOldest({ summarize: summarizeHistory }),\n      }),\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"cleartoolresults","children":[{"type":"text","value":"clearToolResults"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Best for agent loops. Tool output (file reads, command output) is usually most of the tokens. This strategy replaces the content of old tool results with a stub and keeps every message and its tool-call pairing in place. The conversation shape does not change."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { withCompaction, clearToolResults } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  // Keep the 5 most recent tool results in full, stub the older ones.\n  strategy: clearToolResults({ keepRecentToolResults: 5 }),\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"write-your-own","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Write your own"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A strategy is a function. It gets the messages and the budget, and returns the rewritten messages, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" to change nothing. It runs only when the estimate is over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { withCompaction } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\nimport type { CompactionStrategy } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\n// Keep only the last message.\nconst keepLastOnly: CompactionStrategy = (messages) => {\n  if (messages.length <= 1) return null;\n  return messages.slice(-1);\n};\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: keepLastOnly,\n  strategyKey: \"keep-last-v1\",\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strategyKey"},{"type":"text","value":" when you combine a custom strategy with persistence. Change\nthe key when the strategy can produce different output. This prevents an old\ncheckpoint from using stale behavior."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"combine-strategies","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine strategies"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"composeStrategies"},{"type":"text","value":" runs several strategies in order and "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"escalates"}]},{"type":"text","value":": it stops as soon as the result is back under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":". Put the cheap, targeted strategy first and a broad fallback last. Here it clears old tool output first, and only drops old messages if that was not enough."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  withCompaction,\n  composeStrategies,\n  clearToolResults,\n  evictOldest,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: composeStrategies(clearToolResults(), evictOldest()),\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"withcompaction","children":[{"type":"text","value":"withCompaction"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"-"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Compact when the estimated tokens across "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" pass this."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CompactionStrategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"evictOldest()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How to shrink the messages."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"estimateTokens"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(message: ModelMessage) => number"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"characters / 4"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-message token estimate. Pass a real tokenizer if you need exact counts."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strategyKey"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"built-in strategy identity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable checkpoint identity. Set it for custom strategies, custom estimators, or a custom eviction marker. Change it when your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize"},{"type":"text","value":" function can change."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCompact"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(info: CompactionInfo) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"-"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runs after each compaction. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"info"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ before, after, messagesBefore, messagesAfter }"},{"type":"text","value":" (token and message counts)."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"strategy-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy options"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Strategy"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"evictOldest"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keepRecentTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens / 2"},{"type":"text","value":"), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"marker"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarizeOldest"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"required"}]},{"type":"text","value":"), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keepRecentTokens"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summaryRole"},{"type":"text","value":" (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"assistant"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clearToolResults"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keepRecentToolResults"},{"type":"text","value":" (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3"},{"type":"text","value":"), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stub"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The token count is a rough "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"characters / 4"},{"type":"text","value":" estimate. It is good enough to trigger on, not exact. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"estimateTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" for provider-accurate counts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-it-keeps-safe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it keeps safe"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The system prompt is never dropped."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps it separate from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":", so compaction only touches the conversation."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tool calls stay paired with their results."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The built-in strategies never leave an orphaned tool result, so the request stays valid."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It runs before every model call."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Compaction skips "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"init"},{"type":"text","value":". It runs on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeModel"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredOutput"},{"type":"text","value":". Each later call can compact again."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The canonical transcript stays complete."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Compaction writes provider-only context. Persistence and other middleware still read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.messages"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"devtools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DevTools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After a compaction, the chat stream includes three CUSTOM events in order:\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compaction:started"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compaction:state"},{"type":"text","value":", then "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compaction:ended"},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"compaction:started"},{"type":"text","value":" is sent before the strategy runs. Durability flushes each\nevent as soon as it is emitted, so a slow "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarizeOldest"},{"type":"text","value":" call still shows\nas started on the client while it runs. The state and ended events follow when\nthe strategy returns.\nTanStack AI DevTools has a Compaction tab on the hook. Each compact shows:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"started, state, and ended rows"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"when it ran, with token and message counts"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" budget"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"dropped messages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the transcript sent to the model"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The conversation timeline also keeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCompactStart"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCompact"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onCompactEnd"},{"type":"text","value":" steps."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open the AI plugin in the DevTools panel (the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ts-react-chat"},{"type":"text","value":" example mounts it). Select the Compaction hook, then open the Compaction tab."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/compaction"},{"type":"text","value":" route in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-chat"},{"type":"text","value":" uses a small "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTokens"},{"type":"text","value":" so this fires after a few turns. It also uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" (SQLite). Reload after a compact: the chat still shows every message. The banner is example UI, not part of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"compaction-and-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compaction and persistence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compaction and server-side "},{"type":"link","href":"../persistence/chat-persistence","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nuse two message views:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages"},{"type":"text","value":" is the complete canonical transcript. Persistence saves this view."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providerMessages"},{"type":"text","value":" is temporary model context. Compaction rewrites this view."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware order does not change this split. Dropped, summarized, and stubbed\ncontent remains in the message store."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the persistence adapter has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" store, compaction also saves a small\ncheckpoint. The next request validates the canonical prefix, restores the last\ncompacted result, and adds only new messages. A changed prefix or strategy key\ninvalidates the checkpoint."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a checkpoint is reused, a later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarizeOldest"},{"type":"text","value":" pass sees the previous\nsummary plus new messages. Then it folds the old summary into the new one.\nFolding needs a metadata store and a strategy key."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default strategy, standard "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"evictOldest"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarizeOldest"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clearToolResults"},{"type":"text","value":", and safe compositions get a strategy key automatically.\nSet "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strategyKey"},{"type":"text","value":" for custom strategies, custom estimators, or custom marker\nfunctions. Change "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"strategyKey"},{"type":"text","value":" when your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize"},{"type":"text","value":" function can change.\nWithout a metadata store or safe key, compaction stays stateless."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the full hook reference and how middleware composes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./built-in-middleware","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in Middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":": ready-made middleware that ships in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"install","text":"Install","level":2},{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick start","level":2},{"id":"pick-a-strategy","text":"Pick a strategy","level":2},{"id":"evictoldest","text":"evictOldest","level":3},{"id":"summarizeoldest","text":"summarizeOldest","level":3},{"id":"cleartoolresults","text":"clearToolResults","level":3},{"id":"write-your-own","text":"Write your own","level":3},{"id":"combine-strategies","text":"Combine strategies","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"withcompaction","text":"withCompaction","level":3},{"id":"strategy-options","text":"Strategy options","level":3},{"id":"what-it-keeps-safe","text":"What it keeps safe","level":2},{"id":"devtools","text":"DevTools","level":2},{"id":"compaction-and-persistence","text":"Compaction and persistence","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nA long chat or a multi-step agent loop keeps adding messages. At some point the transcript passes the model's context limit and the call fails. You want the conversation to keep working without hitting that wall.\n\n`withCompaction` shrinks provider context before each model call. When the context passes `maxTokens`, a **strategy** rewrites what the model sees. The canonical transcript does not change. Add this [`ChatMiddleware`](./middleware) to the `middleware` array of any `chat()` call.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/ai-compaction\n```\n\n## Quick start\n\nThe default strategy drops the oldest messages once the transcript passes `maxTokens` and keeps the recent ones.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { withCompaction } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withCompaction({ maxTokens: 100_000 })],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Pick a strategy\n\nPass `strategy` to change how the history shrinks. Three are built in.\n\n| Strategy | What it does | Cost |\n|----------|--------------|------|\n| `evictOldest` (default) | Drop the oldest messages, leave a marker | No extra model call |\n| `summarizeOldest` | Replace the oldest messages with an LLM summary | One summarize call |\n| `clearToolResults` | Stub the content of old tool results, keep the messages | No extra model call |\n\n### evictOldest\n\nCheapest. Keeps the recent tail, drops the older head, and leaves a short marker in its place. This is the default, so you only name it to tune `keepRecentTokens`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { withCompaction, evictOldest } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: evictOldest({ keepRecentTokens: 40_000 }),\n});\n```\n\n### summarizeOldest\n\nKeeps the gist of old turns instead of dropping them, at the cost of one summarization call. Pass a `summarize` callback. It gets the messages about to be dropped and returns the summary text. Wire it to `summarize()` or any model call.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, summarize, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText, openaiSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { withCompaction, summarizeOldest } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function summarizeHistory(messages: Array<ModelMessage>): Promise<string> {\n  const text = messages\n    .map((m) => `${m.role}: ${typeof m.content === \"string\" ? m.content : \"\"}`)\n    .join(\"\\n\");\n\n  const { summary } = await summarize({\n    adapter: openaiSummarize(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    text,\n  });\n  return summary;\n}\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [\n      withCompaction({\n        maxTokens: 100_000,\n        strategy: summarizeOldest({ summarize: summarizeHistory }),\n      }),\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n### clearToolResults\n\nBest for agent loops. Tool output (file reads, command output) is usually most of the tokens. This strategy replaces the content of old tool results with a stub and keeps every message and its tool-call pairing in place. The conversation shape does not change.\n\n```typescript\nimport { withCompaction, clearToolResults } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  // Keep the 5 most recent tool results in full, stub the older ones.\n  strategy: clearToolResults({ keepRecentToolResults: 5 }),\n});\n```\n\n### Write your own\n\nA strategy is a function. It gets the messages and the budget, and returns the rewritten messages, or `null` to change nothing. It runs only when the estimate is over `maxTokens`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { withCompaction } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\nimport type { CompactionStrategy } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\n// Keep only the last message.\nconst keepLastOnly: CompactionStrategy = (messages) => {\n  if (messages.length <= 1) return null;\n  return messages.slice(-1);\n};\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: keepLastOnly,\n  strategyKey: \"keep-last-v1\",\n});\n```\n\nSet `strategyKey` when you combine a custom strategy with persistence. Change\nthe key when the strategy can produce different output. This prevents an old\ncheckpoint from using stale behavior.\n\n## Combine strategies\n\n`composeStrategies` runs several strategies in order and **escalates**: it stops as soon as the result is back under `maxTokens`. Put the cheap, targeted strategy first and a broad fallback last. Here it clears old tool output first, and only drops old messages if that was not enough.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  withCompaction,\n  composeStrategies,\n  clearToolResults,\n  evictOldest,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: composeStrategies(clearToolResults(), evictOldest()),\n});\n```\n\n## Options\n\n### withCompaction\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `maxTokens` | `number` | - | **Required.** Compact when the estimated tokens across `messages` pass this. |\n| `strategy` | `CompactionStrategy` | `evictOldest()` | How to shrink the messages. |\n| `estimateTokens` | `(message: ModelMessage) => number` | characters / 4 | Per-message token estimate. Pass a real tokenizer if you need exact counts. |\n| `strategyKey` | `string` | built-in strategy identity | Stable checkpoint identity. Set it for custom strategies, custom estimators, or a custom eviction marker. Change it when your `summarize` function can change. |\n| `onCompact` | `(info: CompactionInfo) => void` | - | Runs after each compaction. `info` is `{ before, after, messagesBefore, messagesAfter }` (token and message counts). |\n\n### Strategy options\n\n| Strategy | Options |\n|----------|---------|\n| `evictOldest` | `keepRecentTokens` (default `maxTokens / 2`), `marker` |\n| `summarizeOldest` | `summarize` (**required**), `keepRecentTokens`, `summaryRole` (default `assistant`) |\n| `clearToolResults` | `keepRecentToolResults` (default `3`), `stub` |\n\nThe token count is a rough `characters / 4` estimate. It is good enough to trigger on, not exact. Pass `estimateTokens` for provider-accurate counts.\n\n## What it keeps safe\n\n- **The system prompt is never dropped.** `chat()` keeps it separate from `messages`, so compaction only touches the conversation.\n- **Tool calls stay paired with their results.** The built-in strategies never leave an orphaned tool result, so the request stays valid.\n- **It runs before every model call.** Compaction skips `init`. It runs on `beforeModel` and `structuredOutput`. Each later call can compact again.\n- **The canonical transcript stays complete.** Compaction writes provider-only context. Persistence and other middleware still read `ctx.messages`.\n\n## DevTools\n\nAfter a compaction, the chat stream includes three CUSTOM events in order:\n`compaction:started`, `compaction:state`, then `compaction:ended`.\n`compaction:started` is sent before the strategy runs. Durability flushes each\nevent as soon as it is emitted, so a slow `summarizeOldest` call still shows\nas started on the client while it runs. The state and ended events follow when\nthe strategy returns.\nTanStack AI DevTools has a Compaction tab on the hook. Each compact shows:\n\n- started, state, and ended rows\n- when it ran, with token and message counts\n- the `maxTokens` budget\n- dropped messages\n- the transcript sent to the model\n\nThe conversation timeline also keeps `onCompactStart`, `onCompact`, and\n`onCompactEnd` steps.\n\nOpen the AI plugin in the DevTools panel (the `ts-react-chat` example mounts it). Select the Compaction hook, then open the Compaction tab.\n\nThe `/compaction` route in `examples/ts-react-chat` uses a small `maxTokens` so this fires after a few turns. It also uses `withPersistence` (SQLite). Reload after a compact: the chat still shows every message. The banner is example UI, not part of `useChat`.\n\n## Compaction and persistence\n\nCompaction and server-side [`withPersistence`](../persistence/chat-persistence)\nuse two message views:\n\n- `messages` is the complete canonical transcript. Persistence saves this view.\n- `providerMessages` is temporary model context. Compaction rewrites this view.\n\nMiddleware order does not change this split. Dropped, summarized, and stubbed\ncontent remains in the message store.\n\nIf the persistence adapter has a `metadata` store, compaction also saves a small\ncheckpoint. The next request validates the canonical prefix, restores the last\ncompacted result, and adds only new messages. A changed prefix or strategy key\ninvalidates the checkpoint.\n\nWhen a checkpoint is reused, a later `summarizeOldest` pass sees the previous\nsummary plus new messages. Then it folds the old summary into the new one.\nFolding needs a metadata store and a strategy key.\n\nThe default strategy, standard `evictOldest`, `summarizeOldest`,\n`clearToolResults`, and safe compositions get a strategy key automatically.\nSet `strategyKey` for custom strategies, custom estimators, or custom marker\nfunctions. Change `strategyKey` when your `summarize` function can change.\nWithout a metadata store or safe key, compaction stays stateless.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Middleware](./middleware): the full hook reference and how middleware composes\n- [Built-in Middleware](./built-in-middleware): ready-made middleware that ships in `@tanstack/ai`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Compaction\nid: compaction\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Keep long chats under the context limit with @tanstack/ai-compaction. withCompaction runs a pluggable strategy before each model call: evict, summarize, or clear old tool output.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - compaction\n  - context window\n  - middleware\n  - token limit\n  - summarize history\n---\n\nA long chat or a multi-step agent loop keeps adding messages. At some point the transcript passes the model's context limit and the call fails. You want the conversation to keep working without hitting that wall.\n\n`withCompaction` shrinks provider context before each model call. When the context passes `maxTokens`, a **strategy** rewrites what the model sees. The canonical transcript does not change. Add this [`ChatMiddleware`](./middleware) to the `middleware` array of any `chat()` call.\n\n## Install\n\n```bash\npnpm add @tanstack/ai-compaction\n```\n\n## Quick start\n\nThe default strategy drops the oldest messages once the transcript passes `maxTokens` and keeps the recent ones.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { withCompaction } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [withCompaction({ maxTokens: 100_000 })],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n## Pick a strategy\n\nPass `strategy` to change how the history shrinks. Three are built in.\n\n| Strategy | What it does | Cost |\n|----------|--------------|------|\n| `evictOldest` (default) | Drop the oldest messages, leave a marker | No extra model call |\n| `summarizeOldest` | Replace the oldest messages with an LLM summary | One summarize call |\n| `clearToolResults` | Stub the content of old tool results, keep the messages | No extra model call |\n\n### evictOldest\n\nCheapest. Keeps the recent tail, drops the older head, and leaves a short marker in its place. This is the default, so you only name it to tune `keepRecentTokens`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { withCompaction, evictOldest } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: evictOldest({ keepRecentTokens: 40_000 }),\n});\n```\n\n### summarizeOldest\n\nKeeps the gist of old turns instead of dropping them, at the cost of one summarization call. Pass a `summarize` callback. It gets the messages about to be dropped and returns the summary text. Wire it to `summarize()` or any model call.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, summarize, toServerSentEventsResponse } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText, openaiSummarize } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\nimport { withCompaction, summarizeOldest } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\nimport type { ModelMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\n\nasync function summarizeHistory(messages: Array<ModelMessage>): Promise<string> {\n  const text = messages\n    .map((m) => `${m.role}: ${typeof m.content === \"string\" ? m.content : \"\"}`)\n    .join(\"\\n\");\n\n  const { summary } = await summarize({\n    adapter: openaiSummarize(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    text,\n  });\n  return summary;\n}\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json();\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n    middleware: [\n      withCompaction({\n        maxTokens: 100_000,\n        strategy: summarizeOldest({ summarize: summarizeHistory }),\n      }),\n    ],\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n### clearToolResults\n\nBest for agent loops. Tool output (file reads, command output) is usually most of the tokens. This strategy replaces the content of old tool results with a stub and keeps every message and its tool-call pairing in place. The conversation shape does not change.\n\n```typescript\nimport { withCompaction, clearToolResults } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  // Keep the 5 most recent tool results in full, stub the older ones.\n  strategy: clearToolResults({ keepRecentToolResults: 5 }),\n});\n```\n\n### Write your own\n\nA strategy is a function. It gets the messages and the budget, and returns the rewritten messages, or `null` to change nothing. It runs only when the estimate is over `maxTokens`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { withCompaction } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\nimport type { CompactionStrategy } from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\n// Keep only the last message.\nconst keepLastOnly: CompactionStrategy = (messages) => {\n  if (messages.length <= 1) return null;\n  return messages.slice(-1);\n};\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: keepLastOnly,\n  strategyKey: \"keep-last-v1\",\n});\n```\n\nSet `strategyKey` when you combine a custom strategy with persistence. Change\nthe key when the strategy can produce different output. This prevents an old\ncheckpoint from using stale behavior.\n\n## Combine strategies\n\n`composeStrategies` runs several strategies in order and **escalates**: it stops as soon as the result is back under `maxTokens`. Put the cheap, targeted strategy first and a broad fallback last. Here it clears old tool output first, and only drops old messages if that was not enough.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  withCompaction,\n  composeStrategies,\n  clearToolResults,\n  evictOldest,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-compaction\";\n\nwithCompaction({\n  maxTokens: 100_000,\n  strategy: composeStrategies(clearToolResults(), evictOldest()),\n});\n```\n\n## Options\n\n### withCompaction\n\n| Option | Type | Default | Description |\n|--------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `maxTokens` | `number` | - | **Required.** Compact when the estimated tokens across `messages` pass this. |\n| `strategy` | `CompactionStrategy` | `evictOldest()` | How to shrink the messages. |\n| `estimateTokens` | `(message: ModelMessage) => number` | characters / 4 | Per-message token estimate. Pass a real tokenizer if you need exact counts. |\n| `strategyKey` | `string` | built-in strategy identity | Stable checkpoint identity. Set it for custom strategies, custom estimators, or a custom eviction marker. Change it when your `summarize` function can change. |\n| `onCompact` | `(info: CompactionInfo) => void` | - | Runs after each compaction. `info` is `{ before, after, messagesBefore, messagesAfter }` (token and message counts). |\n\n### Strategy options\n\n| Strategy | Options |\n|----------|---------|\n| `evictOldest` | `keepRecentTokens` (default `maxTokens / 2`), `marker` |\n| `summarizeOldest` | `summarize` (**required**), `keepRecentTokens`, `summaryRole` (default `assistant`) |\n| `clearToolResults` | `keepRecentToolResults` (default `3`), `stub` |\n\nThe token count is a rough `characters / 4` estimate. It is good enough to trigger on, not exact. Pass `estimateTokens` for provider-accurate counts.\n\n## What it keeps safe\n\n- **The system prompt is never dropped.** `chat()` keeps it separate from `messages`, so compaction only touches the conversation.\n- **Tool calls stay paired with their results.** The built-in strategies never leave an orphaned tool result, so the request stays valid.\n- **It runs before every model call.** Compaction skips `init`. It runs on `beforeModel` and `structuredOutput`. Each later call can compact again.\n- **The canonical transcript stays complete.** Compaction writes provider-only context. Persistence and other middleware still read `ctx.messages`.\n\n## DevTools\n\nAfter a compaction, the chat stream includes three CUSTOM events in order:\n`compaction:started`, `compaction:state`, then `compaction:ended`.\n`compaction:started` is sent before the strategy runs. Durability flushes each\nevent as soon as it is emitted, so a slow `summarizeOldest` call still shows\nas started on the client while it runs. The state and ended events follow when\nthe strategy returns.\nTanStack AI DevTools has a Compaction tab on the hook. Each compact shows:\n\n- started, state, and ended rows\n- when it ran, with token and message counts\n- the `maxTokens` budget\n- dropped messages\n- the transcript sent to the model\n\nThe conversation timeline also keeps `onCompactStart`, `onCompact`, and\n`onCompactEnd` steps.\n\nOpen the AI plugin in the DevTools panel (the `ts-react-chat` example mounts it). Select the Compaction hook, then open the Compaction tab.\n\nThe `/compaction` route in `examples/ts-react-chat` uses a small `maxTokens` so this fires after a few turns. It also uses `withPersistence` (SQLite). Reload after a compact: the chat still shows every message. The banner is example UI, not part of `useChat`.\n\n## Compaction and persistence\n\nCompaction and server-side [`withPersistence`](../persistence/chat-persistence)\nuse two message views:\n\n- `messages` is the complete canonical transcript. Persistence saves this view.\n- `providerMessages` is temporary model context. Compaction rewrites this view.\n\nMiddleware order does not change this split. Dropped, summarized, and stubbed\ncontent remains in the message store.\n\nIf the persistence adapter has a `metadata` store, compaction also saves a small\ncheckpoint. The next request validates the canonical prefix, restores the last\ncompacted result, and adds only new messages. A changed prefix or strategy key\ninvalidates the checkpoint.\n\nWhen a checkpoint is reused, a later `summarizeOldest` pass sees the previous\nsummary plus new messages. Then it folds the old summary into the new one.\nFolding needs a metadata store and a strategy key.\n\nThe default strategy, standard `evictOldest`, `summarizeOldest`,\n`clearToolResults`, and safe compositions get a strategy key automatically.\nSet `strategyKey` for custom strategies, custom estimators, or custom marker\nfunctions. Change `strategyKey` when your `summarize` function can change.\nWithout a metadata store or safe key, compaction stays stateless.\n\n## Next steps\n\n- [Middleware](./middleware): the full hook reference and how middleware composes\n- [Built-in Middleware](./built-in-middleware): ready-made middleware that ships in `@tanstack/ai`\n"}
